# No patches · no leftovers · no workarounds

Owner standing order (2026-08-05). The owner will audit the whole app. Do not ignore this.

## Forbidden

- Stopgap “patches” that paper over bugs instead of fixing the real cause
- Workarounds (`history.back()` loops, `replace` used only to hide bad stacking when named exits were never defined, `stopPropagation` / z-index / `pointer-events` wars to make a broken control clickable)
- Leftover dead code, duplicate handlers, commented-out experiments, temp files, unused CSS, or half-reverted UI hacks
- Fake success, silent catch-and-ignore on real flows, or client shims that mask wrong contracts
- Piecemeal one-screen hacks when the owner asked for app-wide behavior (e.g. silver–red writing, close button placement)
- “Quick fix now, clean later” — there is no later

## Required

- One clear contract: named routes/parents for exit navigation, one close handler, one writing style system
- Fix the root cause in place (structure the header so close is not inside a drag capture; navigate to a named parent — not patch around it)
- If a prior change left leftovers or conflicting hacks, remove them in the same task
- Prefer a small honest redesign of the broken control/flow over stacking more guards

## When unsure

- Stop and ask before inventing another workaround
- Stability and owner rules over speed

Default: **proper fix only. No patches. No leftovers. No workarounds.**
